 r←ListOpenProjects verboseFlag;res;aliases;ind;noOfObjectsCol
 '⍵ must be a Boolean'Assert(⊂verboseFlag)∊0 1
 r←(0(2+2×verboseFlag))⍴''
 res←⎕SE.Link.Status''
 ({1=≡,⍵:⍵ ⋄ 1↓⊃,/(⎕UCS 13),¨⍵}res)Assert~∨/'ERRORS ENCOUNTERED:'⍷∊res
 :If 'No active links'≢res
⍝ The column is found by its header rather than by position, and it must be found before the header
⍝ row is dropped. Link 3 (Dyalog 18.2) reports three columns, "Namespace | Directory | Files"; Link 4
⍝ (19.0 and later) inserted one for the direction arrow and renamed "Directory" to "Source". A fixed
⍝ index therefore meant the number of objects under Link 3 and the source folder under Link 4.
     noOfObjectsCol←res[1;]⍳⊂'Files'
     :If 0<≢res←(∧/'Namespace' 'Files'∊res[1;])↓res   ⍝ Will become superfluous with a proper Link API but doesn't do damage
         'Link demands a Resync!'Assert~∨/'Link.Resync required'⍷∊res
     :AndIf 0<≢res←({⊃9=⍵.⎕NC'CiderConfig'}∘⍎¨res[;1])⌿res
         r←res[;,1],({6::'' ⋄ (⍎⍵).CiderConfig.HOME}¨res[;1])
         :If verboseFlag
             r,←res[;noOfObjectsCol]
         :EndIf
         r←(0<≢¨r[;2])⌿r
         r[;2]←DropTrailingSlash¨r[;2]
         r[;2]←F.EnforceSlash¨r[;2]
         :If verboseFlag
             :If 0<≢aliases←GetCiderAliasFileContent ⍬
                 aliases[;2]←DropTrailingSlash¨aliases[;2]
             :AndIf 0<≢aliases←(aliases[;2]∊r[;2])⌿aliases
                 r,←⊂''
                 ind←r[;2]⍳aliases[;2]
                 r[ind;4]←aliases[;1]
             :Else
                 r,←⊂''
             :EndIf
         :EndIf
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
